# C2 three-phase heap_malloc shot (4.4.4) — evidence §42

# Purpose: close the seam §41 left open. §41 tagged heap_malloc only on ENTRY ('M'), so the live
# `new_rt MMM` could not separate "died inside the 3rd HeapAlloc" (heap/environment side) from
# "died in QuickJS's own code between two allocations" (engine side) — the two §36 hypotheses.
# This shot writes a MATCHED PAIR per malloc: 'M' on entry, then 'm' (HeapAlloc returned a block) or
# '!' (returned NULL). A dangling 'M' (nothing after it) is the positive signature of "the allocation
# call never returned."
# Binary question this answers: did our allocator RETURN the three allocations it was entered for?
# exe identity: stellaris.exe 4.4.4 sha256 9242c40abb78b53e88039ead1270ad82eb003959fb2d413c856d280ea02b1a56 (46,253,688 bytes)
# DLL instrumented: stellaris_quickjs.dll (build.zig default x86_64-windows target), deployed as
#   C:\temp\sqjs_c42.dll. Tooling change is commit c90a8e2 (heap_malloc three-phase + the offline
#   no-dangling-M positive-control test in c2_diag_test.zig).

